1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Level one,

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:05,640
the rookie.

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:08,560
You are 21 years old. You work the night

4
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:10,240
shift at a gas station. The pay is bad.

5
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:12,320
The hours are worse.

6
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,840
You live in your mother's basement. She

7
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:16,000
raised you alone after your father

8
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:17,320
walked out. You have a younger brother

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,920
named Danny.

10
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:21,240
He is 15 and he looks up to you.

11
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:25,080
You don't know what you want from your

12
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:27,000
life. You feel stuck and you feel small.

13
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:30,280
Then one night, a man walks into the

14
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,040
station. He is huge. He wears a black

15
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:35,520
vest that says agent across the back.

16
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:37,800
He buys a coffee and a pack of gum.

17
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:39,680
You ask him what kind of agent he is.

18
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,720
He tells you he hunts people who skip

19
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:43,160
bail.

20
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:45,400
He chases fugitives for money.

21
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,640
You have never heard of such a thing.

22
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:49,480
You ask him a hundred questions. He

23
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:50,520
laughs and slides a card across the

24
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:53,520
counter.

25
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:55,800
The card says bail enforcement. He tells

26
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:57,960
you to come by his office on Monday.

27
00:00:55,800 --> 00:01:00,280
You don't sleep that night. You think

28
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:01,640
about chasing criminals for a living.

29
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:03,920
You think about doing something that

30
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:06,520
finally matters.

31
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:08,360
On Monday, you show up an hour early.

32
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:11,880
The office is a cramped room above a

33
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:13,440
pawn shop. The man's name is Frank.

34
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,800
Frank is 60 and built like a

35
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:17,320
refrigerator. He has done this work for

36
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,920
30 years.

37
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:21,080
He looks you up and down. He asks if you

38
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:23,960
can run.

39
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:26,040
He asks if you can fight. He asks if you

40
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:27,400
can stay calm when a man is screaming in

41
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:30,400
your face.

42
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:31,920
You say yes to all of it. You were lying

43
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:34,440
about most of it.

44
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:37,200
Frank knows you were lying. He hires you

45
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:39,640
anyway. He says everyone lies on day

46
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:41,840
one. He says the job teaches you the

47
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:44,240
truth fast.

48
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:46,880
Your first task is paperwork.

49
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:49,000
You learn how bail actually works.

50
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:50,920
Someone gets arrested. They cannot

51
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,880
afford to stay in jail.

52
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:53,880
A bondsman pays the court to release

53
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,680
them.

54
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,760
The defendant promises to show up for

55
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,800
trial.

56
00:01:56,760 --> 00:02:01,000
Many of them never do.

57
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:02,000
When they run, the bondsman loses his

58
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,960
money.

59
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,960
That is where you come in.

60
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:09,399
You find the runner. You bring him back.

61
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:11,520
The bondsman pays you a percentage.

62
00:02:09,399 --> 00:02:13,240
It is a strange business built on broken

63
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:15,920
promises.

64
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:18,400
You ride along with Frank for 3 months.

65
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:20,200
You watch everything he does.

66
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,440
You carry the gear and keep your mouth

67
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,959
shut.

68
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:26,400
You learn how Frank knocks on a door.

69
00:02:23,959 --> 00:02:27,680
You learn how he talks a scared man into

70
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,480
the truck.

71
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:32,400
You were at the very bottom of this

72
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:34,520
world. You make almost nothing.

73
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:36,680
But for the first time in your life, you

74
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:38,920
wake up excited.

75
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:40,640
You tell Danny about it over dinner.

76
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:42,120
He thinks his big brother is becoming a

77
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,560
real hunter.

78
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:46,480
You start to believe it, too.

79
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:48,080
On your third week, Frank lets you knock

80
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:49,880
on a door alone.

81
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:51,280
A woman answers and lies straight to

82
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:53,200
your face.

83
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:54,480
You can see in her eyes that her son is

84
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:56,280
inside.

85
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:57,840
You back off because Frank told you to

86
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:59,680
be patient.

87
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:01,280
That night, the man slips out a window

88
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:03,360
and runs.

89
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:05,040
Frank is not angry with you.

90
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:07,360
He says you will lose more men than you

91
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:10,120
catch at first. He says the ones who

92
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:12,720
quit never learn that lesson.

93
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:14,120
You decide right then that you will not

94
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:17,120
quit.

95
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:18,600
Level two, the licensed agent.

96
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:21,600
Frank tells you it is time to get

97
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:23,920
licensed. Every state is different. Some

98
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:26,400
require a course and a background check.

99
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:28,480
Some require almost nothing at all.

100
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:29,640
Yours requires a class and a clean

101
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:31,280
record.

102
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:32,440
You take the course at night after your

103
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:34,680
shifts.

104
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:37,120
You learn the laws of arrest. You learn

105
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:39,200
what you can and cannot do.

106
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,959
A bounty hunter holds powers a regular

107
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:42,560
citizen does not.

108
00:03:40,959 --> 00:03:44,000
In many states, you can enter a

109
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,560
fugitive's home.

110
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,800
You can cross state lines to make a

111
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:48,519
capture.

112
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:50,239
The fugitive signed those rights away on

113
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:52,239
the bail contract.

114
00:03:50,239 --> 00:03:54,400
But you learn the limits, too.

115
00:03:52,239 --> 00:03:56,640
You cannot break down the wrong door.

116
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:59,160
You cannot grab the wrong man.

117
00:03:56,640 --> 00:04:00,400
One mistake can injure career or your

118
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:02,560
freedom.

119
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:04,080
You pass the course. Your license

120
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:05,920
arrives in the mail.

121
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:07,200
It feels like a diploma you actually

122
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:09,240
earned.

123
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:10,320
Frank takes you on your first real solo

124
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,840
skip.

125
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:14,760
The target missed his court date for

126
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:16,519
theft. He is not dangerous.

127
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:18,239
He is just scared and hiding at his

128
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:19,959
girlfriend's apartment.

129
00:04:18,239 --> 00:04:22,400
You knock on the door.

130
00:04:19,959 --> 00:04:23,960
Your heart pounds against your ribs.

131
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:25,760
The man answers.

132
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:28,120
You tell him who you are.

133
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:29,600
You tell him he has to come with you.

134
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:31,800
He bolts.

135
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:34,200
You chase him across a parking lot.

136
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:36,640
You tackle him onto the hood of a car.

137
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:38,320
You cuff him with shaking hands.

138
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:39,480
Frank watches the whole thing from the

139
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:41,400
truck.

140
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:43,440
He says you did fine.

141
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:45,800
He says you talk too much.

142
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:48,160
A good hunter says less.

143
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:50,440
You drive the man back to the jail. You

144
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:53,480
collect your first real paycheck.

145
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:55,120
It is $800 for 2 hours of work.

146
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:56,280
You have never held that much cash at

147
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:58,080
once.

148
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:59,280
Around this time, you meet a woman named

149
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:01,600
Maria.

150
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:03,880
She works at a diner near the office.

151
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:06,160
She thinks your job is insane.

152
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:08,840
She agrees to a date anyway.

153
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:10,240
You like her more than you expected to.

154
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:11,640
You tell her you are going to be the

155
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:14,040
best at this.

156
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:15,880
She laughs and tells you to prove it.

157
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:17,560
You fully intend to.

158
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,600
You spend the next 2 years building a

159
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:21,160
name.

160
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:23,400
You take the cases nobody else wants.

161
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:25,400
You knock on a thousand doors.

162
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,680
You catch men hiding in attics and crawl

163
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:28,240
spaces.

164
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,720
You learn that finding people is the

165
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:32,440
real skill.

166
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:34,800
Anyone can make an arrest. Not everyone

167
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:36,600
can find the person to arrest.

168
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,919
You send Danny part of every paycheck

169
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,400
for college.

170
00:05:37,919 --> 00:05:40,960
Your mother tells the neighbors what her

171
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:43,560
son does now.

172
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:45,919
For the first time, she sounds proud.

173
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:48,880
That changes something inside you.

174
00:05:45,919 --> 00:05:50,840
You decide this is no longer just a job.

175
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:53,560
This is who you are.

176
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:56,000
Level three, the skip tracer.

177
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:58,000
You realize the chase is the easy part.

178
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,920
The hard part is the hunt.

179
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,520
Most fugitives are not hiding in plain

180
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:05,360
sight. They go underground. They change

181
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:07,960
phones. They borrow names. They sleep on

182
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:10,040
couches and move every few nights.

183
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:11,560
Finding them is a puzzle.

184
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,600
You decide to become great at the

185
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:15,000
puzzle.

186
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:17,680
You learn skip tracing. It is the art of

187
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:19,840
finding people who refuse to be found.

188
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:22,120
You build yourself a system. You start

189
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:23,360
with the bail application. It is full of

190
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:26,240
information.

191
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:29,600
Family members, old employers, previous

192
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:32,000
addresses, phone numbers, references.

193
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:34,280
People always lie on these forms. But

194
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,640
the lies point somewhere. You learn to

195
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:37,760
read between them.

196
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:40,720
You call the mother first. You never

197
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:42,120
threaten her. You are polite and calm.

198
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,880
You tell her you just want to help her

199
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:45,440
son turn himself in.

200
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:47,760
Half the time she gives him up without

201
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:50,400
realizing it. She mentions where he used

202
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:52,800
to work. She mentions an old girlfriend.

203
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:54,680
She mentions a cousin in another town.

204
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,960
You write all of it down.

205
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:58,280
You learn to use databases. You pull

206
00:06:56,960 --> 00:07:00,680
utility records and vehicle

207
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:02,440
registrations. You search social media

208
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:04,800
for hours at a time.

209
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:07,320
People cannot stay off their phones. A

210
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:09,480
fugitive posts one photo and forgets the

211
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:11,000
background gives away the street.

212
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:12,000
You notice the things other hunters

213
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,840
miss.

214
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,840
You once track a man using only his

215
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:17,400
girlfriend's pizza deliveries.

216
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:19,800
You learn the deep patterns of human

217
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:20,840
behavior. People always return to what

218
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:22,560
they know.

219
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:24,520
They go back to their mother. They go

220
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:26,560
back to their old neighborhood. They go

221
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:29,240
back to the person they love.

222
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:30,840
A man can change his name. A man cannot

223
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:32,400
change his habits.

224
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:35,040
You catch a fugitive who has been gone

225
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:36,800
for two full years. You find him because

226
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:39,560
he always orders the same brand of

227
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:41,760
cigarettes. A clerk remembers the face

228
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:43,400
and the corner store gives him away.

229
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:46,200
The bondsman tells you that three other

230
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:47,920
hunters had already given up. You smile

231
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:50,000
and you take the check.

232
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:52,400
By now, you have married Maria.

233
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,560
The wedding was small and cheap. Frank

234
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:55,880
stood beside you as your best man.

235
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,920
You buy a little house on the edge of

236
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:58,720
town.

237
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:59,720
Maria worries every time you leave for

238
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:01,440
work.

239
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:03,560
You tell her you are careful.

240
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:05,760
You are mostly telling the truth.

241
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:08,000
Your reputation keeps growing. Other

242
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:10,400
bondsmen start calling you directly.

243
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:12,720
They have a runner that nobody can find.

244
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:14,400
They have heard that you find anyone.

245
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:15,600
You take their hardest cases and you

246
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:17,080
close them.

247
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:18,040
You are not the strongest hunter in the

248
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,800
city.

249
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:21,520
You are the smartest one.

250
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:24,440
You find men who have been ghosts for

251
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:25,680
years. The money gets better. The cases

252
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:27,520
get harder.

253
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:29,080
And the harder cases bring a new kind of

254
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:32,320
danger.

255
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:34,599
Level four, the fugitive recovery agent.

256
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:36,520
The easy skips are behind you now. You

257
00:08:34,599 --> 00:08:38,039
hunt the dangerous ones.

258
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:40,400
These are not scared kids who missed a

259
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:43,960
court date. These are violent men with

260
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:46,280
serious charges. Armed robbery, assault,

261
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:47,400
drug trafficking. Men who will not come

262
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:49,000
quietly.

263
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:50,200
Men who would rather fight than go back

264
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,920
inside.

265
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:54,480
The bondsmen pay far more for these

266
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:55,839
captures. They pay more because the risk

267
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:57,880
is real.

268
00:08:55,839 --> 00:09:00,320
You train harder than ever.

269
00:08:57,880 --> 00:09:02,040
You learn to handle a firearm properly.

270
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:04,000
You learn defensive tactics and how to

271
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:05,720
control a struggling man.

272
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,920
You learn to wear a vest every single

273
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:09,440
time.

274
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:12,080
Frank drills one rule into your head.

275
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:13,640
Never go in alone if you can avoid it.

276
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:14,760
You start bringing back up on the bad

277
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,760
ones.

278
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:17,800
Your first truly dangerous capture goes

279
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:19,960
wrong.

280
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:22,280
The target is wanted for assault.

281
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:23,760
You track him to a motel on the highway.

282
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:25,640
You kick the door.

283
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:27,280
He is waiting with a knife.

284
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,480
He slashes your forearm before you can

285
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,960
tackle him.

286
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:32,400
You wrestle the blade away and pin him

287
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:33,680
down. You cuff him while blood runs down

288
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:35,280
your sleeve.

289
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:36,960
You drop him at the jail and drive

290
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:38,640
yourself to the hospital.

291
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:41,000
You get 12 stitches.

292
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:42,880
Maria cries when she sees the bandage.

293
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,120
She begs you to quit.

294
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:46,360
You don't.

295
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:49,120
You tell her this is who you are now.

296
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:50,800
That scar becomes the first of many.

297
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,600
You learn to read a door before you open

298
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:53,200
it.

299
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:54,960
You learn that the arrest itself is the

300
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:57,240
most dangerous moment.

301
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:59,440
A cornered man is unpredictable.

302
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:01,520
You learn to talk before you fight.

303
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:02,760
Words capture more men than force ever

304
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:03,920
will.

305
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:06,200
You learn to give a man a way to

306
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:07,760
surrender without losing his pride.

307
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:09,520
Most of them take it.

308
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:11,160
The ones who don't teach you to always

309
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:13,480
be ready.

310
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:15,360
Around this time your daughter is born.

311
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,680
You name her Sophia.

312
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:18,760
You hold her in the hospital and

313
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:20,600
something shifts inside you.

314
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:22,000
You think about the knife.

315
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:23,280
You think about the men who chose to

316
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,960
fight.

317
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:27,120
You wonder for the first time if this

318
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:29,200
job will let you grow old.

319
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:31,440
But you have a family to feed now.

320
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:33,360
The dangerous cases pay the bills, so

321
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:35,080
you keep kicking doors.

322
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:37,640
You become known as the man who closes

323
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:39,120
the cases other hunters refuse.

324
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:41,360
Word of that spreads further than you

325
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:43,720
expect. And the people who hear it have

326
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:46,200
much bigger work to offer.

327
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:48,480
Level five, the team leader.

328
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:50,120
You cannot keep doing this alone.

329
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:52,520
The hardest captures need more than one

330
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:53,880
man. So you build a team.

331
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:56,160
You recruit hunters you trust

332
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:58,520
completely. A tracker who is better at

333
00:10:56,160 --> 00:11:00,000
databases than you are. A young muscle

334
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:01,120
named Reggie who reminds you of

335
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,560
yourself.

336
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:05,000
A woman named Dana who can talk anyone

337
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:06,960
out of a house.

338
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:09,120
You become the leader of the crew. You

339
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:11,800
plan the operations. You assign the

340
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:14,360
roles. You are responsible now for more

341
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:15,920
than your own life. You are responsible

342
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:17,800
for theirs.

343
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:20,040
You learn that leading is harder than

344
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:21,600
hunting. A good hunter only has to

345
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:23,839
control himself.

346
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:25,280
A leader has to control a whole team

347
00:11:23,839 --> 00:11:27,000
under pressure.

348
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:29,920
You run surveillance for days before a

349
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:32,600
capture. You map the target's house. You

350
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:35,200
know every door and every window. You

351
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,720
know who is inside and when.

352
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:40,160
You brief your team before every

353
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:41,720
operation. You leave nothing to chance.

354
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:44,040
Frank taught you that planning is what

355
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:46,360
keeps people alive. You learn to trust

356
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:48,720
your people with your life.

357
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:50,320
On one capture, Dana talks a man down

358
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:52,160
who is holding a bat.

359
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:53,280
She keeps him calm while Reggie moves in

360
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:55,320
behind him.

361
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:56,520
Nobody throws a punch and nobody gets

362
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:58,920
hurt.

363
00:11:56,520 --> 00:12:00,560
You realize a good team is worth more

364
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:02,680
than any weapon.

365
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:04,760
You take down a major target. He is

366
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:07,000
wanted for armed robbery across three

367
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:08,680
counties. You watch his routine for a

368
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,400
full week.

369
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:13,240
You take him in his driveway at dawn

370
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:16,560
before he is awake. No shots fired,

371
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:17,800
nobody hurt. It is clean and fast and

372
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:20,600
professional.

373
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:22,920
The bondsman pays you $20,000.

374
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:24,760
You split it fairly with your team.

375
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:27,800
You build the kind of crew that bondsman

376
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:28,760
request by name. Your phone never stops

377
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:31,160
ringing.

378
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:33,320
You turn down more work than you accept.

379
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:34,920
You only take the cases that are worth

380
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:37,880
the risk.

381
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:39,680
At home, Sophia is 4 years old now. She

382
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:41,080
calls you daddy and runs to the door

383
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:43,440
when you come home.

384
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:45,040
Maria has stopped asking you to quit.

385
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,960
She has made a quiet peace with the

386
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:48,200
fear.

387
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:49,720
She just asks you to come home every

388
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:51,680
single time.

389
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:54,360
You promise her that you will.

390
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:56,440
It is a promise you cannot truly keep.

391
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:57,920
But you make it anyway because she needs

392
00:12:56,440 --> 00:13:00,000
to hear it.

393
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:02,320
You are good at this work. You are maybe

394
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,600
the best in your entire region.

395
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,839
You start to notice something that

396
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:07,080
bothers you.

397
00:13:04,839 --> 00:13:10,040
The men who pay you make far more than

398
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:12,120
you do. The bondsman takes the big cut.

399
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:13,960
You take all the risk.

400
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:16,200
You start to wonder why you don't own

401
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:18,839
the whole operation yourself.

402
00:13:16,200 --> 00:13:21,000
The thought refuses to leave you alone.

403
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:23,120
You talk it over with Maria one night.

404
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:25,560
She tells you to bet on yourself.

405
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:28,040
You decide that she is right.

406
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:30,320
Level six, the agency owner.

407
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:32,280
You stop working for other people. You

408
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:35,760
build your own business from the ground

409
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:37,720
up. You earn your bail bondsman license.

410
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:40,320
Now you don't just catch the runners.

411
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:42,720
You write the bonds in the first place.

412
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:45,040
You open a real office this time, not a

413
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:48,160
room above a pawn shop, a clean

414
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:50,520
storefront with your name on the glass.

415
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:52,680
You hire staff. You have hunters who

416
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:53,720
work for you the way you once worked for

417
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:55,400
Frank.

418
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:57,560
The whole operation runs through you

419
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:59,920
now. You understand the business from

420
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:01,240
both ends. You know which defendants are

421
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:03,120
likely to run.

422
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:05,760
You read people in your office the way

423
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:08,200
you read fugitives in the field. You can

424
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:10,680
tell who will show up to court. You can

425
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:11,720
tell who is lying about a job they don't

426
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:13,600
have.

427
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:15,720
You charge accordingly.

428
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:17,240
The risky ones pay a higher premium or

429
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:18,880
bring a co-signer.

430
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:21,880
It is a numbers game and you have

431
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:23,200
learned the numbers cold. Some clients

432
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:24,840
still run.

433
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:27,560
That is simply the cost of doing

434
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:30,040
business. But now when they run, you

435
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:32,200
already know everything about them. You

436
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:34,760
wrote the bond yourself. You have their

437
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:36,920
whole life sitting in a folder.

438
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:39,120
You send your own team after them. You

439
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:41,360
catch almost everyone.

440
00:14:39,120 --> 00:14:44,320
Your recovery rate becomes the best in

441
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:47,520
the state. The money is different now.

442
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:49,440
It is not $800 for a single chase. It is

443
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:51,960
a steady river of premiums and

444
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:54,760
recoveries and contracts. You buy a

445
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:57,400
bigger house. Sophia gets her own room

446
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:59,200
with a window facing the yard. Maria

447
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:01,320
finally quits the diner.

448
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:03,839
You take a real vacation for the first

449
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:05,240
time in a decade. But the weight is

450
00:15:03,839 --> 00:15:07,800
heavier, too.

451
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:09,600
You have a payroll to meet every month.

452
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:12,280
You have hunters whose families depend

453
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:14,440
on the work. You have lawyers to pay and

454
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:16,960
a business that never sleeps.

455
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:19,800
Frank visits the office sometimes. He is

456
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:21,560
old now and slow on his feet. He looks

457
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:23,040
around at everything you built and

458
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:24,760
shakes his head.

459
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:27,360
He says he never imagined the kid from

460
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:29,040
the gas station owning all this.

461
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,880
You tell him he is the one who built

462
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:33,120
you.

463
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:35,360
He says no. He says you built yourself.

464
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:38,080
He says he just opened the door.

465
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:40,440
A year later, Frank dies in his sleep.

466
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:42,760
You give the eulogy at his funeral.

467
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,720
You realize that you are the old man

468
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:45,160
now.

469
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:46,440
And there is still bigger game out

470
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:49,720
there.

471
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:52,320
Level seven, the high-value hunter.

472
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:54,720
Local skips no longer interest you. You

473
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:57,000
go after the big ones. The high-value

474
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:59,280
fugitives. The men who have been running

475
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,960
for years. The ones with rewards

476
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:02,640
attached to their names.

477
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:04,800
Some of these bonds are worth hundreds

478
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:07,280
of thousands of dollars. The bondsman

479
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:09,760
who wrote them is desperate. He will pay

480
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:11,480
enormous sums to get the man back.

481
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:13,640
You take these cases because no one else

482
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:15,720
can close them. These fugitives are

483
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:18,080
professionals at vanishing. They have

484
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:19,760
money. They have fake documents. They

485
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:21,440
cross state lines and sometimes

486
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:22,880
international borders.

487
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:25,160
You follow them across the entire

488
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:27,480
country. You learn to work in cities you

489
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:29,280
have never seen. You build a network in

490
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:30,760
nearly every state.

491
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:33,040
You have contacts in dozens of

492
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:35,200
jurisdictions. Local hunters who feed

493
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:37,640
you tips. Sources buried inside

494
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:39,040
neighborhoods. People who owe you favors

495
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,839
and pay them back.

496
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:42,160
You spend weeks away from home chasing a

497
00:16:40,839 --> 00:16:43,880
single man.

498
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:46,240
You track one fugitive from Texas to

499
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:47,720
Arizona. Then you track him to a small

500
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:49,520
town in Mexico.

501
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:52,480
You cannot operate legally across that

502
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:54,080
border. So you work with people who can.

503
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:56,240
You coordinate with local authorities

504
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:58,560
and you wait. You wait for the man to

505
00:16:56,240 --> 00:17:00,760
cross back over. You take him the moment

506
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:02,200
he sets foot on American soil. The

507
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,400
payout is a quarter of a million

508
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:05,040
dollars.

509
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:07,600
On another case, you spend a month in a

510
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:09,319
city you hate. You sit in a parked car

511
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,319
watching an apartment for hours every

512
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:12,600
day.

513
00:17:10,319 --> 00:17:13,920
You eat cold food and you sleep 2 hours

514
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:15,920
at a time.

515
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:17,520
When the man finally appears, you take

516
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:19,520
him in under a minute.

517
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,760
The waiting is the job now, not the

518
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:22,120
chase.

519
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:24,360
You have become something more than a

520
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:26,920
bounty hunter. You are a specialist that

521
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:29,440
people fly across the country to hire.

522
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:32,040
But the work eats your life alive.

523
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:34,760
You are gone far more than you are home.

524
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:36,680
Sophia is a teenager now. She is furious

525
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:38,480
that you missed her birthday again.

526
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:40,280
She tells you that you love the chase

527
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:42,200
more than you love her.

528
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:43,360
The words cut deeper than any knife ever

529
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:46,080
did.

530
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:47,360
Maria has grown quiet and far away.

531
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:48,720
The fear in her has turned into

532
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:50,520
distance.

533
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:52,400
You sleep in hotel rooms in cities whose

534
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:53,760
names blur together.

535
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:54,840
You catch the most wanted men in the

536
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:57,080
country.

537
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:59,360
You cannot catch up to your own family.

538
00:17:57,080 --> 00:18:00,680
You tell yourself the money is worth it.

539
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:02,200
You tell yourself you are building

540
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:03,760
something for them.

541
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:05,680
But you come home one day and the house

542
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:07,120
feels like a place you visit.

543
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:08,800
You start to understand that every

544
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:10,240
capture has a price.

545
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:12,440
And the price is being paid by the

546
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:15,560
people you love most.

547
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:17,400
Level eight, the federal contractor.

548
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:19,520
Your reputation reaches the highest

549
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:20,440
levels. The government takes notice of

550
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,360
you.

551
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:23,840
Federal agencies need people who can

552
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:25,160
find fugitives that have vanished

553
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:27,400
completely.

554
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:29,560
The marshals are overworked. Cases go

555
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:31,320
cold and stay cold.

556
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:32,640
They start using private contractors for

557
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:34,280
certain work.

558
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:35,760
You become one of them.

559
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:38,000
You are no longer chasing men who

560
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:40,760
skipped a small bond. You are hunting

561
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:43,280
fugitives wanted across the nation.

562
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:45,600
You work alongside task forces now. You

563
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:47,960
sit in briefings with federal agents.

564
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:49,640
You bring skills that they do not have.

565
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:51,040
You think like a hunter, not a

566
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:53,120
bureaucrat.

567
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:54,160
You go places that a badge cannot easily

568
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:55,760
go.

569
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:58,240
You knock on doors that an official

570
00:18:55,760 --> 00:19:00,160
agency needs a warrant to approach.

571
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:02,240
You operate in the gray space between

572
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:03,840
the law and the street.

573
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:05,880
You find a fugitive who eluded the

574
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:08,240
marshals for six years.

575
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:10,680
You do it in three weeks.

576
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:12,920
You used the oldest trick you know.

577
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:14,160
You found the woman he loved and you

578
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:16,320
