733
00:24:08,240 --> 00:24:13,320
You are still paying for it.

734
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:17,080
Then, one ordinary afternoon, the phone

735
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:19,400
rings. It is Sophia. She is 26 now and

736
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:21,000
she is getting married in the spring.

737
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:22,760
She wants to know if her father will

738
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:25,000
walk her down the aisle.

739
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:26,400
You sit down hard because your legs will

740
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:28,600
not hold you.

741
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:29,920
You say yes before she even finishes the

742
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:32,080
sentence.

743
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:35,160
You hang up the phone and you cry for

744
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:36,880
the first time in 30 years.

745
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:39,400
You spent your entire life hunting

746
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:41,720
strangers and you finally caught the one

747
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:44,680
thing you actually wanted.

748
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:46,920
Somewhere, right now, a young man is

749
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:48,520
working a dead-end job and dreaming of

750
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:51,200
something more.

751
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:54,120
A man with a vest and a story will walk

752
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:56,240
into his life and hand him a card.

753
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:58,080
He will not sleep that night.

754
00:24:56,240 --> 00:25:01,360
He will not know what the job will give

755
00:24:58,080 --> 00:25:03,000
him or what it will quietly take.

756
00:25:01,360 --> 00:25:06,520
He will not know about the doors it

757
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:08,200
opens or the ones it closes forever.

758
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:10,120
He will learn.

759
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:13,840
They always do.

760
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:13,840
The cycle continues.

